{
  "title": "DeepSeek R1: Implications for AI",
  "authors": [
    "Sarah Mercer",
    "Samuel Spillard",
    "Daniel P. Martin"
  ],
  "year": 2025,
  "arxivId": "2502.02523",
  "abstract": "The release of DeepSeek R1, a reasoning model developed at a fraction of the cost of comparable models, has significant implications for the field of Generative AI. This report discusses the model, its capabilities, and the potential consequences of its release, including the impact on the AI industry, potential security risks, and the role of reinforcement learning in its development.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "The Core Idea",
      "content": "DeepSeek R1 is a reasoning model that uses <strong>Reinforcement Learning (RL)</strong> to improve its performance on mathematical and coding tasks. The model is based on the DeepSeek V3 model, which employs a <strong>Mixture of Experts (MoE)</strong> architecture to reduce training costs. By using RL, the model can learn to generate more tokens and explore alternative approaches, leading to emergent behaviors such as <strong>self-reflection</strong>.",
